    "text": "To determine the total number of red colored pencils Johnny bought, we need to break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of red pencils in the 12 packs:**\n   Each pack contains 1 red pencil. Therefore, the number of red pencils in the 12 packs is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ packs} \\times 1 \\text{ red pencil per pack} = 12 \\text{ red pencils}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of red pencils in the 3 extra packs:**\n   Each of these 3 packs contains 2 extra red pencils. Therefore, the number of red pencils in these 3 packs is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ packs} \\times 2 \\text{ red pencils per pack} = 6 \\text{ red pencils}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of red pencils:**\n   Add the number of red pencils from the 12 packs to the number of red pencils from the 3 extra packs:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ red pencils} + 6 \\text{ red pencils} = 18 \\text{ red pencils}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of red colored pencils Johnny bought is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
